.TH JTUTIL-PICOROM "1" "November 2026" "jtutil-picorom manual" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jtutil-picorom \- PicoROM-based PCB work: load, verify, probe, power and bus tests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jtutil picorom units
.br
.B jtutil picorom load
\fINAME\fR=\fIIMAGE\fR... [\fB\-\-size\fR 64k|128k|256k] [\fB\-\-xgecu\fR] [\fB\-\-bench\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.br
.B jtutil picorom read
\fINAME FILE\fR [\fB\-\-length\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B jtutil picorom rename
\fIOLD NEW\fR
.br
.B jtutil picorom probe
\fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-seconds\fR 8s] [\fB\-\-interval\fR 50ms] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B jtutil picorom power
status|on|off
.br
.B jtutil picorom bustest
show|gen|sim|run|report \fIcore\fR [\fIset\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Drives PicoROM ROM emulators plugged into the program ROM sockets of an arcade
PCB. It talks to the units through Linux usbfs (no libusb), loads and verifies
images, switches the PCB supply and runs CPU bus timing tests whose results can be
compared with the FPGA core in
.BR jtsim .
.PP
Every command accepts
\fB\-\-json\fR
for machine-readable output and
\fB\-\-lab\fR \fIFILE\fR
to use another laboratory file. Exit status: 0 done, 1 error, 3 a PCB run did not
complete.
.SH LABORATORY FILE
\fB$JOTEGO/picorom.yaml\fR
describes the local setup and is not part of the repository:
.PP
.nf
units:                    # key: USB chip serial (see "units")
  E6614103E7123456: {name: unit1, pins: 32, note: "diagnostic firmware"}
  E6614103E7654321: {name: unit2, pins: 32, disabled: "pin 2 shorted to GND"}
power:                    # omit for a manual switch
  type: shelly-gen2
  url: http://192.0.2.10
  id: shellyplugsg3-0123456789ab
  switch: 0
  interface: wlo1         # optional: bind the HTTP requests to this NIC
programmer:
  minipro_device: "AM27C010@DIP32"
.fi
.PP
A unit with a \fBdisabled\fR reason is never loaded. Without a power section the
person at the bench is asked to switch the supply, which needs a terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B units
Lists connected units with their build, diagnostic firmware, address mask, whether
they have the event recorder (diagnostic firmware) and the lab entry.
.TP
.B load
Writes each image into the unit's volatile memory and reads every byte back. The
PCB must be off: with a power switch this is checked; otherwise
\fB\-\-yes\fR confirms it, and \fB\-\-bench\fR skips it when no unit is in a PCB.
\fB\-\-size 64k\fR ignores A16 and up. \fB\-\-xgecu\fR also reads the single unit
through the XGecu programmer socket. The report keeps the field names of the earlier
picorom_load.py tool.
.TP
.B read
Saves the unit's current image.
.TP
.B rename
Changes the unit's name, kept in its flash. Replug its cable if it does not come back
on USB.
.TP
.B probe
Powers the PCB for a bounded time and samples the address, /CE and /OE pins of a unit
with the diagnostic firmware. Constant address lines with the socket never selected
mean a stuck CPU: all ones usually means a tri-stated bus (reset, halt, no clock);
another value is a cycle waiting for DTACK.
.TP
.B power
Reads or switches the PCB supply.
.SH BUS TESTS
The test for a set is defined in
\fBcores/\fIcore\fB/cfg/picorom.yaml\fR
under \fBbustest:\fR, and its files go to
\fBcores/\fIcore\fB/ver/\fIset\fB_bustest/\fR
(ignored by Git). The program times 256 iterations of a four-access loop per case,
three times, between marker reads that the recorder unit timestamps.
.TP
.B show
Describes the test, or lists the core's sets when only the core is given.
.TP
.B gen
Generates the program (test.s), the ROM lane images and manifest.json.
.TP
.B sim
Replaces the program ROM in a copy of the core's ROM, runs jtsim with
\fB\-d SIM_HOOK\fR and a generated sim_hook.h that logs the marker reads, and writes
sim_result.json. Needs rom/\fIset\fR.rom (jtframe mra \fIcore\fR).
.TP
.B run
Prints the placement and checklist, waits for confirmation (\fB\-\-yes\fR once the
board is ready), checks power is off, loads every lane, arms the recorder, powers the
PCB, acknowledges each case and switches the PCB off. The recorder unit serves the
marker lane; \fB\-\-unit\fR \fIlane\fR=\fINAME\fR overrides the choice.
\fB\-\-stall\-probe\fR samples the recorder pins when the markers stop.
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the plan only.
.TP
.B report
Compares the latest PCB run with the jtsim result as a Markdown table.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
jtutil picorom units
jtutil picorom power status
jtutil picorom bustest show riders glfgreat
jtutil picorom bustest sim riders glfgreat
jtutil picorom bustest run riders glfgreat --dry-run
jtutil picorom bustest report riders glfgreat
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
$JTFRAME/doc/picorom.md,
.BR jtsim (1)
